  - MUTATE F_OperationAuthorisation  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OperationAuthorisation.als
    rationale: F_OperationAuthorisation is the sole fact that ties Operation.outcome=Success to the permission matrix. Clearing it allows successful operations outside the allow-set, which LeastPrivilege and every role-scope predicate must catch.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerLimited, FR_003_LoanOfficerPermissions, FR_004_ComplianceReadOnly, FR_005_OnlyCustomersSubmit, FR_023_ComplianceNoWrite
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_002_CustomerLimited: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_003_LoanOfficerPermissions: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_004_ComplianceReadOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_005_OnlyCustomersSubmit: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_023_ComplianceNoWrite: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the structural ban on duplicate audit entries for the same (application, prevStatus, newStatus) transition. The injection forces two distinct entries to coexist, which the AppendOnly assertion must catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_018_AuditAppendOnly, FR_019_ExactlyOneAuditPerChange
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_018_AuditAppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_019_ExactlyOneAuditPerChange: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditMatchesStatus  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditMatchesStatus.als
    rationale: F_AuditMatchesStatus is the sole fact linking each application's status to the existence of the corresponding audit entries. Clearing it lets an application reach Approved without any UnderReview→Approved record, which AuditCompleteness must surface.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_017_AuditPerStatusChange
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditPerStatusChange: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnershipBasedCustomerAccess  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_OwnershipBasedCustomerAccess.als
    rationale: This fact restricts customer-GetApplication successes to applications the caller owns. Removing it allows a customer to successfully view someone else's application, which OwnershipBasedAccess must catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_020_CustomerOwnOnly
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_020_CustomerOwnOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NoInformationLeakage  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_NoInformationLeakage.als
    rationale: Removes the rule that customers asking about a non-owned application receive NotFound (not PermissionDenied). The injection forces a leakage instance which NoInformationLeakage must catch.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: F_AuditAttribution enforces actor↔transition correspondence. Clearing it lets an initial-submission audit entry record an actor other than the application's customer, which AttributionCorrectness must catch.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_009_InitialSubmissionRecorded, FR_011_ClaimTransitionRecorded
